* b_ldo_loop_native.cir -- SAME LDO-style loop as
* docs/examples/a_ldo_loop_lgprobe.cir, broken at the SAME wire, but with
* the probe written as a single existing 0 V V-source (native `.stb`'s
* probe=<Vname> only resolves a plain voltage-source instance -- it does
* not expand the stb/lgprobe.lib subcircuit, so "Vprobe fb fbtop DC 0"
* replaces "XP fb fbtop lgprobe" here). Electrically this is the same
* break: lgprobe.lib's Vi/Ii/Vb are themselves a 0 V branch with the same
* a=downstream/b=upstream roles (see stb/lgprobe.lib and
* tests/test_stb_native.py's check_dc_identical, which checks this
* equivalence bit-for-bit on the DC operating point). docs/stb.md example
* (b) -- run against the private fork build (buildrecipe/README.md), not
* the system ngspice.
*
* Run (interactive `stb` command, control block below), or as a netlist
* card:
*   .stb dec 30 10 10meg probe="Vprobe"
* (quoted -- see docs/stb.md's syntax reference for why the netlist-card
* form needs quotes and the interactive command does not).

.param gm1=5m rp1=1meg cp1=100p cfb=2p
.param gm2=400m rout=3.3 esr=50m cout=47u
.param rf1=68k rf2=12k

Vref vref 0 DC 0 AC 0
G1 0 ea vref fb {gm1}
Rp1 ea 0 {rp1}
Cp1 ea 0 {cp1}
Cfb fb 0 {cfb}

Vin vin 0 DC 5 AC 0
G2 vin vout ea 0 {gm2}
Rout vout 0 {rout}
Cout vout esrnode {cout}
Resr esrnode 0 {esr}

Rf1 vout fbtop {rf1}
Rf2 fbtop 0 {rf2}

Vprobe fb fbtop DC 0

* No wrdata below on purpose -- this deck's job is the printed phase/gain
* margin lines (STBan()'s own stdout output), which need no output file at
* all. docs/stb.md's example (b) numbers come straight from that output.
* A run that also wants the T(f)/loopgain(f) trace would add, e.g.,
*   wrdata <absolute path under ~/Work/data/ngspice_augmentation/...> stb1.t
* -- never a bare relative filename, which would land inside this repo.
.control
stb dec 30 10 10meg probe=Vprobe
quit
.endc
.end

